// Plain org membership never implies repo admin. The README states repo
// admin comes from either a direct grant or organization.repo_admin
// (itself independently grantable — "Users can have repository admin
// access on organizations, and thus have admin access to all
// repositories owned by that organization") — never from mere
// organization membership on its own. repo#admin's rewrite closure
// (admin_direct | owner->repo_admin) never references organization
// member_direct at all, so this is semantically a genuine
// unreachability claim — type-level, the same shape as this tool's own
// no-public-path-to-private-document fixture.
//
// Before `docs/DECISIONS.md`'s entry adding `NeverRelationConstraint`,
// this invariant's own real verdict was VIOLATED, not the HOLDS its
// intent describes above: nothing stopped the search from adding one
// more, wholly unconstrained direct grant of `admin_direct` (bare
// principal) — the exact "recurring finding" `docs/FINDINGS.md`
// disclosed — and even after excluding that one specific grant (D-131's
// `not admin_direct(r) = s`), a second, structurally different escape
// through `admin_direct`'s own `team#member` userset-subject branch
// remained, and a completely separate third escape through
// `organization.repo_admin`'s own bare grant. `never repo#admin_direct(s)`
// closes both of `admin_direct`'s own branches at once (bare and
// userset-subject — see `NeverRelationConstraint`'s own doc comment for
// why blocking the whole relation, not one candidate tuple, is what's
// needed); `never organization#repo_admin(s)` closes the third,
// independent escape the same way. See `docs/FINDINGS.md` for the full
// account.
invariant plain_org_member_never_gets_repo_admin {
  s: user
  o: organization
  r: repo

  member_direct(o) = s
  owner(r) = o

  never repo#admin_direct(s)
  never organization#repo_admin(s)

  goal: admin(s, r)
}
